# What must not ship inside the release zip.
#
# scripts/build.sh copies from an allow-list, so this is the second layer: it
# prunes strays from inside the directories that do ship, vendor/ most of all.
#
# Directory entries are anchored with a leading slash on purpose. rsync matches
# an unanchored pattern at any depth, and an unanchored `src` once shipped a
# sibling plugin's only runtime dependency as a lone LICENSE file.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.distignore
.editorconfig
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.husky
.nvmrc
.linchpin.json
.phplint.yml
.php-cs-fixer.dist.php
.php-cs-fixer.cache
.phpunit.cache
.stylelintrc.json
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
commitlint.config.js
composer.lock
package.json
package-lock.json
eslint.config.js
webpack.config.js
phpcs.xml.dist
phpstan.neon
phpunit.xml
renovate.json
release-please-config.json
.release-please-manifest.json
/src
/dev
/tests
/docs
/plans
/playground
/scripts
/test-results
/playwright-report
# WordPress.org listing assets. Both 10up actions copy this directory to the
# SVN /assets tree themselves; it never belongs in trunk or the zip.
/.wordpress-org
# Repository-facing artwork: the GitHub social preview and the logo sources.
/assets
/node_modules
/blocks/node_modules
/blocks/src
/blocks/package.json
/blocks/package-lock.json
/blocks/webpack.config.js
/blocks/eslint.config.js
/blocks/.stylelintrc.json
/CHANGELOG.md
